/**
 * Place for user defined web analytics software codes/tags
 *
 * Tools like Matomo and Google Analytics normally provide a small HTML code
 * snippet ("tag") which you have to include on your website to make everything
 * work. This template tries to make this easier for you.
 *
 * You do not have to decide where to paste the code;
 * simply create a "/user/tracker.php" file. The template recognizes and loads
 * the provided tracker data automatically. You may want to rename this file
 * from "tracker.php.dist" to "tracker.php" to get a good starting point.
 * Add only trusted administrator-provided PHP output code below. For raw HTML,
 * use echo or a heredoc so this PHP-only file can omit the closing tag.
 *
 * The contents are emitted as raw template output, so do not paste untrusted
 * user-provided data here.
 *
 * Note: All example files are delivered with the ".dist" extensions to make
 *       sure your changes do not get overwritten when updating the template.
 *       Just remove the ".dist" extension to use them.
